   "rule": "The <strong>dual</strong> adds <span class='ar'>ـَانِ</span> (-āni) to the singular. It already means “two”, so no number is needed. ة opens into ت: <span class='ar'>سَاعَةٌ</span> → <span class='ar'>سَاعَتَانِ</span>. “These two” is <span class='ar'>هَذَانِ</span> (m) or <span class='ar'>هَاتَانِ</span> (f), and “they two” is <span class='ar'>هُمَا</span>."
